{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"Databricks.DatabricksCLI","latestVersion":"1.25.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Databricks Command Line Interface","license":"DB license","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Databricks Command Line Interface","license":"DB license","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","name":"DatabricksCLI","packageUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli","publisher":"Databricks","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/issues","publisherUrl":"https://databricks.com/","releaseNotes":"CLI\n- databricks aitools install --output json now reports a more specific error_category (MANIFEST_NOT_FOUND, PERMISSION_DENIED, FILESYSTEM) for some failures it reported as UNCATEGORIZED. (#7380)\n- Suggest databricks auth logout --profile <profile-name> --delete when multiple profiles match the same workspace in databricks auth docker commands. (#7363)\n- Fix %pip in Jupyter notebooks opened over databricks ssh connect on serverless environment versions 5 and 6 and on dedicated clusters running recent Databricks Runtime versions, which fell back to the stock IPython magic instead of the Databricks one. (#7263)\nAI Runtime\n- databricks air run now validates the config server-side while it uploads the run artifacts, instead of before, which shortens submission. (#7368)\n- Remove CRITICAL as a valid compute.priority_class value; the AI Runtime API no longer accepts it. (#7371)\nBundles\n- Built-in templates add the workspace ID to workspace.host (?w=<id>) when the profile or an environment variable sets it, so generated bundles select the right workspace on hosts shared by several workspaces. Welcome messages show the same URL, and dbt-sql also adds ?o=<id> to the HTTP path it suggests for dbt init. (#7350)\n- Fix grants of a renamed or recreated catalog, schema, volume or other UC resource staying recorded under the old name, which made the next bundle plan propose to apply them again. (#7345)\n- Fix permissions of a recreated pipeline, app, dashboard, model serving endpoint or other resource staying recorded under the old ID, which made every later bundle plan propose to apply them again. (#7361)\n- Add the postgres_data_apis resource (Private Preview) for enabling and configuring the Data API of a Lakebase Postgres database. (#7160)\n- Fixes #4012: registered model aliases are now set in Unity Catalog on deploy instead of being silently ignored. A model without an aliases section keeps the aliases set outside the bundle (for example by MLflow), and aliases: [] removes them. (#7163)\n- Include variable declarations and the source of each resolved value in the --include-locations output of bundle validate and bundle summary. (#7351)\n- Add .workspace.URLID to bundle templates: the workspace ID that .workspace.URL adds, or empty, so templates can use it without failing when the ID is unknown. (#7388)\n- Expose the workspace of the selected profile to bundle templates as .workspace, with Hostname, ID, and URL, so templates can address a workspace on a host shared by several workspaces. A template input named workspace takes precedence. (#7349)\nDependency Updates\n- Bump dependencies with known vulnerabilities. (#7394)\n- Upgrade github.com/mattn/go-runewidth to v0.0.31, which removes ~30ms of startup time from every command. (#7391)\n- Update the Go SDK to v0.194.0. (#7371)\n- Update the Go SDK to v0.195.0. (#7384)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/releases/tag/v1.25.0","tags":["command-line-interface","databricks"]}},"name":"DatabricksCLI","packageUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli","publisher":"Databricks","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/issues","publisherUrl":"https://databricks.com/","releaseNotes":"CLI\n- databricks aitools install --output json now reports a more specific error_category (MANIFEST_NOT_FOUND, PERMISSION_DENIED, FILESYSTEM) for some failures it reported as UNCATEGORIZED. (#7380)\n- Suggest databricks auth logout --profile <profile-name> --delete when multiple profiles match the same workspace in databricks auth docker commands. (#7363)\n- Fix %pip in Jupyter notebooks opened over databricks ssh connect on serverless environment versions 5 and 6 and on dedicated clusters running recent Databricks Runtime versions, which fell back to the stock IPython magic instead of the Databricks one. (#7263)\nAI Runtime\n- databricks air run now validates the config server-side while it uploads the run artifacts, instead of before, which shortens submission. (#7368)\n- Remove CRITICAL as a valid compute.priority_class value; the AI Runtime API no longer accepts it. (#7371)\nBundles\n- Built-in templates add the workspace ID to workspace.host (?w=<id>) when the profile or an environment variable sets it, so generated bundles select the right workspace on hosts shared by several workspaces. Welcome messages show the same URL, and dbt-sql also adds ?o=<id> to the HTTP path it suggests for dbt init. (#7350)\n- Fix grants of a renamed or recreated catalog, schema, volume or other UC resource staying recorded under the old name, which made the next bundle plan propose to apply them again. (#7345)\n- Fix permissions of a recreated pipeline, app, dashboard, model serving endpoint or other resource staying recorded under the old ID, which made every later bundle plan propose to apply them again. (#7361)\n- Add the postgres_data_apis resource (Private Preview) for enabling and configuring the Data API of a Lakebase Postgres database. (#7160)\n- Fixes #4012: registered model aliases are now set in Unity Catalog on deploy instead of being silently ignored. A model without an aliases section keeps the aliases set outside the bundle (for example by MLflow), and aliases: [] removes them. (#7163)\n- Include variable declarations and the source of each resolved value in the --include-locations output of bundle validate and bundle summary. (#7351)\n- Add .workspace.URLID to bundle templates: the workspace ID that .workspace.URL adds, or empty, so templates can use it without failing when the ID is unknown. (#7388)\n- Expose the workspace of the selected profile to bundle templates as .workspace, with Hostname, ID, and URL, so templates can address a workspace on a host shared by several workspaces. A template input named workspace takes precedence. (#7349)\nDependency Updates\n- Bump dependencies with known vulnerabilities. (#7394)\n- Upgrade github.com/mattn/go-runewidth to v0.0.31, which removes ~30ms of startup time from every command. (#7391)\n- Update the Go SDK to v0.194.0. (#7371)\n- Update the Go SDK to v0.195.0. (#7384)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/databricks/cli/releases/tag/v1.25.0","tags":["command-line-interface","databricks"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.25.0/app.json","detailSha256":"fc7442a823920a7eca2264cf30a89d5d0c459d4546be25eded64f212d6806b06","releaseDate":"2026-11-10","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"1.25.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.24.0/app.json","detailSha256":"c610a3c2fee6ed5f94859f2d7c4627f99f771308d22d6a5cd2507b074ab3b36b","releaseDate":"2026-11-04","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.24.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.22.1/app.json","detailSha256":"3537bd19837e75396cee5f5d197cf22d42506b8dbccb0bdf52aeecc3df5e1e50","releaseDate":"2026-10-22","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.22.1"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.22.0/app.json","detailSha256":"753b472774754afcc7b5557c313b00146b1d986be1bab87cfecec16ae46ecc45","releaseDate":"2026-10-22","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"1.22.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/1.21.0/app.json","detailSha256":"1f46c356bcda80a4f9bc5c071b930